<PolicyLayout title="Terms of use" description="Use the evidence, check its limits, and respect the people who contribute to the commons.">
  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>Developing Country brings public socioeconomic datasets, maps, and research together. These terms apply to developing-country.org, explore.developing-country.org, and the Developing Country MCP tools. Questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:team@developing-country.org">team@developing-country.org</a>.</p>

  <h2>Accounts and connected tools</h2>
  <p>You must be at least 13 years old to create an account. Keep your account access secure. Authorize an AI client only if you trust it to use the tools and information available through your account. Review requests before sharing private notes or locations. You are responsible for the content you submit and the actions you authorize through connected clients, and you can disconnect a client at any time in its own settings.</p>

  <h2>Evidence and decisions</h2>
  <p>Datasets can contain gaps, errors, estimates, or outdated observations. Check the source, date, coverage, and limitations before relying on a result. Maps and analysis are informational and do not replace official records, professional advice, or a site inspection. Verify information independently before consequential decisions. An AI assistant that uses these tools writes its own answers and can misread or misstate a result, so check its figures against the cited source.</p>

  <h2>Reuse and attribution</h2>
  <p>Third-party datasets and map services retain their own licences and attribution requirements. Follow the licence and source notes for each dataset you reuse. Public availability does not by itself grant permission to reuse every item. Cite the source and relevant dataset version when sharing findings.</p>

  <h2>Shared content</h2>
  <p>Submit information you have the right to share. Do not post confidential information, another person's private details, unlawful material, or misleading content. Prospects you make public and views you share are publicly visible and may be displayed through the website and tools. Contact the maintainer if shared content needs correction or removal.</p>

  <h2>Responsible access</h2>
  <p>Do not attempt to access another user's private records, bypass authentication or rate limits, disrupt the service, or misuse credentials. Access may be restricted to protect users and keep the service available.</p>

  <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>The service and its features can change or become unavailable. We do not guarantee uninterrupted availability or the completeness or accuracy of every result. These terms do not remove rights or protections that cannot lawfully be excluded. Updated terms will be posted here with a revised date.</p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains account information, Google sign-in, saved activity, shared content, and connected AI clients.</p>
</PolicyLayout>
